{"type":"Film","id":"ES2020_072","slug":"es2020-072-el-verano-que-vivimos","title":{"native":"El verano que vivimos","english":""},"release":{"type":"Theatrical release","date":"2020-12-04","year":2020},"filmType":"Fiction film","directors":[{"id":"Carlos Sedes","slug":"carlos-sedes","name":"Carlos Sedes","birthYear":1973,"deathYear":0,"gender":"Male identifying","nationality":"Spain","awards":[]}],"genre":["Drama","Romance","Historical film (Heritage Film)"],"media":{"posterUrl":"https://www.imdb.com/title/tt10042590/mediaviewer/rm265921537/?ref_=tt_ov_i","trailerUrl":"https://www.imdb.com/title/tt10042590/?ref_=nv_sr_srsg_1_tt_7_nm_0_in_0_q_El%2520verano%2520que%2520vivimos"},"synopsis":{"native":"Año 1998. Isabel, estudiante de periodismo, se ve obligada a realizar sus prácticas en el diario de un pequeño pueblo costero gallego para terminar la carrera. Al llegar, quiere empezar cuanto antes a investigar, a demostrar todo lo que ha aprendido para convertirse en una auténtica periodista. Pero el puesto que le asignan es el último que ella esperaba: la escritura y gestión de las esquelas que llegan a la redacción. Pero esto, que podría parecer en principio algo aburrido, se convierte en la puerta a una investigación que la llevará por diferentes puntos de la geografía española en busca de una historia de amor imposible.","english":"Isabel is a journalism student who is in the journal of a Galician coastal town for her work placement. During her stay, she finds an anonymous obituary dedicated to Lucía. It tells a love, friendship and treason story in 1958."},"production":[{"country":"Spain","share":"Majority coproducer"}],"characters":[{"id":"ES2020_072_01","film":"ES2020_072","person":{"id":"Manuel Morón","slug":"manuel-moron","name":"Manuel Morón","birthYear":1956,"deathYear":0,"gender":"Male identifying","nationality":"Spain","awards":[]},"age":"3: Third Age (60-75)","gender":"Male identifying","sexuality":"Unknown","origin":"White Western European","class":"Unkn